WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:22.666
"Whew! It sure is hot today," Henry's friend Cole said.

2
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:25.857
"That's why we're getting ice cream, remember?"

3
00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:28.473
Henry pointed to a shop just ahead.

4
00:00:28.474 --> 00:00:31.110
It was called the Sweet Shop.

5
00:00:31.111 --> 00:00:35.569
A board on the sidewalk outside listed the store's special flavors.

6
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:42.660
"Today's special flavors are raspberry mint chip and bubble gum banana swirl," Cole read aloud.

7
00:00:42.661 --> 00:00:45.245
"Maybe I'll try bubble gum banana swirl.

8
00:00:45.246 --> 00:00:51.227
No . . . Wait, I think I'll get marshmallow fudge. That's my favorite."

9
00:00:51.228 --> 00:00:56.850
A bell over the door jingled when Henry and Cole entered the ice-cream shop.

10
00:00:56.851 --> 00:00:59.369
Several people were waiting in line.

11
00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.045
The woman behind the counter looked up when she heard the bell.

12
00:01:03.046 --> 00:01:07.795
"Hello, boys," she said. "I'll be with you shortly."

13
00:01:07.796 --> 00:01:10.720
"Thanks, Mrs. Sweet," Henry said.

14
00:01:10.721 --> 00:01:15.198
Everyone in Belltown liked Mrs. Sweet and her homemade ice cream.

15
00:01:15.199 --> 00:01:19.046
She had owned the Sweet Shop since Henry's parents were babies.

16
00:01:19.047 --> 00:01:22.684
The shop never changed much, but the flavors did.

17
00:01:22.685 --> 00:01:25.863
Mrs. Sweet was always inventing new ones.

18
00:01:25.864 --> 00:01:29.768
Henry and Cole waited until it was their turn to be served.

19
00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:35.787
"I'll try one scoop of raspberry mint chip in a cone, please," Henry said.

20
00:01:35.788 --> 00:01:38.788
"Marshmallow fudge for me," Cole said.

21
00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:42.951
"Coming right up, boys."

22
00:01:42.952 --> 00:01:47.899
Mrs. Sweet picked up two cones and leaned into the cooler to get the ice cream.

23
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.602
Henry looked around. "This place is busy today."

24
00:01:52.603 --> 00:01:54.609
"It sure is.

25
00:01:54.610 --> 00:02:00.847
Hot weather always makes people want a nice cool treat!" Mrs. Sweet winked.

26
00:02:00.848 --> 00:02:06.125
"But you must know that already. How's business at your lemonade stand?"

27
00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.327
"Great," Henry said.

28
00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:13.082
"That reminds me, we promised to bring back some ice cream for Maggie."

29
00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:20.758
Cole nodded. "She wants a scoop of cherry vanilla in a cup."

30
00:02:20.759 --> 00:02:24.841
Soon Henry and Cole were back outside with their ice cream.

31
00:02:24.842 --> 00:02:28.123
"We'd better hurry," Henry said.

32
00:02:28.124 --> 00:02:32.247
"We promised Maggie we'd be back soon to help with the customers."

33
00:02:32.248 --> 00:02:37.411
"Yeah." Cole licked his ice cream, which was already starting to melt in the heat.

34
00:02:37.412 --> 00:02:46.338
"Besides," he added, "Maggie will be mad if her ice cream melts before we get back."

35
00:02:46.339 --> 00:02:51.743
Half a dozen people were clustered around the lemonade stand when Henry and Cole reached it.

36
00:02:51.744 --> 00:02:54.375
Maggie saw the two boys coming.

37
00:02:54.376 --> 00:03:00.056
"Hurry up, you two!" she called. "I can't do everything by myself!"

38
00:03:00.057 --> 00:03:05.613
"Sorry. We tried to hurry." Henry ate the last bite of his ice-cream cone.

39
00:03:05.614 --> 00:03:10.549
Then he handed Maggie her ice cream and grabbed a pitcher of lemonade.

40
00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:13.972
"Who's next?" he called to the customers.

41
00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:17.060
"I am," a familiar voice said.

42
00:03:17.061 --> 00:03:21.118
"Dad!" Henry looked up and saw his father grinning at him.

43
00:03:21.119 --> 00:03:23.513
"What are you doing here?"

44
00:03:23.514 --> 00:03:28.924
"Are you writing a story about our lemonade stand, Uncle Kevin?" Maggie joked.

45
00:03:28.925 --> 00:03:33.978
Henry's father chuckled. He was a reporter for the local newspaper.

46
00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:37.881
"Nope," he said. "I'm just here for lemonade."

47
00:03:37.882 --> 00:03:41.991
As Henry handed his father a cup, an older man arrived.

48
00:03:41.992 --> 00:03:45.666
"Well, hello, Kevin," he greeted Henry's father.

49
00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:50.945
"Mr. Moss!" Henry's dad smiled. "I've been meaning to call you.

50
00:03:50.946 --> 00:03:55.516
You did a great job fixing our garage door last weekend."

51
00:03:55.517 --> 00:04:00.819
"One lemonade, please," Mr. Moss said to Henry, handing him a quarter.

52
00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.450
Then he turned back to Henry's father.

53
00:04:03.451 --> 00:04:07.045
"I'm glad you're pleased with the repair job," he said.

54
00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:13.027
"Speaking of garages, did you hear about Mr. O'Malley's new car?"

55
00:04:13.028 --> 00:04:17.334
The two men wandered away with their lemonade, still chatting.

56
00:04:17.335 --> 00:04:21.309
"Mr. Moss fixed your garage door?" Cole asked Henry.

57
00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.431
"I thought he was an art teacher."

58
00:04:23.432 --> 00:04:29.694
"He retired last year," Maggie told him. "Now he does odd jobs around town.

59
00:04:29.695 --> 00:04:34.639
My parents hired him to paint our garden shed, and they said he did a great job."

60
00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:40.890
She grinned. "Except he likes to chatter while he works about things going on around town."

61
00:04:40.891 --> 00:04:44.937
"Mr. Moss loves to gossip," Henry agreed.

62
00:04:44.938 --> 00:04:48.774
Cole looked around. "Whew!" he said.

63
00:04:48.775 --> 00:04:51.754
"That's the last of our customers for right now."

64
00:04:51.755 --> 00:04:57.485
"Yeah," Maggie said. "The lemonade stand has been really busy all day."

65
00:04:57.486 --> 00:05:03.288
She glared at the boys. "Especially while you two were gone."

66
00:05:03.289 --> 00:05:07.727
Henry grinned. "Having more customers means we make more money."

67
00:05:07.728 --> 00:05:12.872
"That's true." Maggie looked happier. "I need all the money I can get.

68
00:05:12.873 --> 00:05:16.561
I'm still saving up to enter the horse show at my barn.

69
00:05:16.562 --> 00:05:20.543
And we're not making much from our detective business these days."

70
00:05:20.544 --> 00:05:26.586
"True." Henry nodded. "We haven't had a new case in a few days."

71
00:05:26.587 --> 00:05:29.179
Cole helped himself to some lemonade.

72
00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.495
"You're right. Maybe we've solved all the mysteries in Belltown!"

73
00:05:33.496 --> 00:05:36.126
"Maybe," Henry said.

74
00:05:36.127 --> 00:05:41.408
Maggie looked worried. "I hope not. Entering that horse show is expensive."

75
00:05:41.409 --> 00:05:46.069
"Here comes another customer." Cole pointed down the street.

76
00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:51.950
"Who is it?" When Henry turned to look, he saw a young man he didn't recognize.

77
00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:54.400
A moment later the man reached them.

78
00:05:54.401 --> 00:05:56.988
But he didn't even glance at the lemonade.

79
00:05:56.989 --> 00:06:00.455
"Are you the kid detectives I've heard about?" he demanded.

80
00:06:00.456 --> 00:06:09.234
"Because I need someone to help me prove something—my ice-cream flavor was stolen!"
